  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Message-boundary governance intercepts text entering shared context c_t; it does not enforce RBAC/sandboxing on external tool calls already executed mid-turn, nor does role consistency guarantee factual accuracy, completeness, or safety (§8).",
    "Adapting ATC to a new domain requires manually authoring role descriptions, role-consistent demonstrations, speech-act masks b_i, and logical contracts C_i=(O_i, B_i); Appendix A4.5 notes demo counts, predicate counts, and curation hours are omitted from the PDF, and exact S1-S3 model checkpoints plus L/S classifier details reside in repository configs.",
    "Evaluation uses predefined static roles (10-12 roles) and an automated fixed-rubric Judge(y_{i,t}, r_i) without human validation or multi-judge robustness checks (§8); 3-seed means omit standard deviation/CI intervals; CAA/SEA baselines assume white-box activation access unavailable for closed APIs.",
    "Proposition 3 (Eq. 12) guarantees local monotonicity only on the pre-regeneration continuous vector objective, not on post-regeneration realized text D_ling/D_logic (Appendix A1.4); excessive lambda (2.00) triples harmful over-correction from 5.6% to 18.4% (Table 15).",
    "Subagent close reading audited extracted primary text (1,183 lines) and verified arXiv/GitHub metadata without locally executing ATC rollouts or verifying SHA-256 hashes (deferred to parent under run_command ban)."
  ],
